IMPORT prelude

-- ISEAS - Yusof Ishak Institute Act 1968 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for a person dealing with the Institute: the shield
-- from personal liability (s 17), how donations must be registered and applied (s 16), when an instrument is validly sealed
-- (s 10), who may demand fees and on what footing (s 14(2)(d)(vii), (h)), who inspects committee records (s 14(4)), and which
-- body decides which matter (ss 5, 5A, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15); and, for those inside it, Board membership, terms, vacancies and
-- meetings (ss 4, 6) and the Executive Committee's size and quorum (s 13).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/ISEASYIIA1968.txt. The deposit says the revised
-- edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the
-- latest amending Act annotated in the text and the Legislative History is Act 5 of 2018 (Public Sector (Governance) Act 2018,
-- in force 1 April 2018). The ARRANGEMENT OF SECTIONS agrees with the body for this Act.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0179 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has
-- asked a sharper question yet. The Act turns out to create no offence and no penalty; what it decides for an outsider is
-- narrow. Not encoded: the Institute's object (s 3), the Board's general powers (s 5) beyond who decides what, Ministerial
-- directions (s 5A) beyond who gives them, contracts, property, borrowing and investment (ss 8, 9), shares to the Minister for
-- Finance (s 9A), the content of the Executive Committee's regulation-making heads (s 14(2)(d), (e)) other than fees, pensions
-- and residences (s 14(2)(f), (g)), and the rule-making power's heads (s 15(2)). No regulations made by the Executive Committee
-- and no rules made by the Minister were retrieved, so no actual fee is known.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `ISEAS - Yusof Ishak Institute Act 1968 -- the Institute and the public`

§§ `17 -- protection from personal liability`

-- s 17: "No liability is to lie personally against any member of the Board, employee of the Institute or other person acting
-- under the direction of the Institute who, acting in good faith AND with reasonable care, does or omits to do anything in --
-- (a) the exercise or purported exercise of any power under this Act; or (b) the performance or purported performance of any
-- function or duty under this Act."
-- Good faith alone is not enough: careless conduct in good faith is outside the shield. The section protects the person; it says
-- nothing about the Institute's own liability.
GIVEN `is a Board member, Institute employee or person acting under the Institute's direction` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `acted with reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `in the exercise or performance, actual or purported, of a power, function or duty under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the personal liability shield applies` IF
        `is a Board member, Institute employee or person acting under the Institute's direction`
    AND `acted in good faith`
    AND `acted with reasonable care`
    AND `in the exercise or performance, actual or purported, of a power, function or duty under the Act`

§§ `16 -- gifts and donations`

-- s 16(1): the Board may accept "by way of grant, gift, testamentary disposition or otherwise, property and moneys in aid of the
-- finances of the Institute on any conditions that it may determine".
-- (2): "Registers must be kept of ALL donations to the Institute, including the names of donors and any special conditions on
-- which any donation may have been given." No exception for a donor who asks to stay anonymous is written in.
-- (3): "All property, moneys or funds donated for any specific purposes must be applied and administered in accordance with the
-- purposes for which they have been donated and must be separately accounted for."
-- That a donation given for no specific purpose may be applied to any purpose of the Institute is an inference from s 16(1)
-- ("in aid of the finances of the Institute") read with s 16(3).
GIVEN `the donor asked to stay anonymous` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the donor's name must be entered in the register` IF TRUE

GIVEN `donated for a specific purpose` IS A BOOLEAN, `the proposed use is that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the donation may be applied to the proposed use` IF
        (NOT `donated for a specific purpose`)
    OR  `the proposed use is that purpose`

GIVEN `donated for a specific purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the donation must be separately accounted for` IF `donated for a specific purpose`

§§ `10 -- use of the common seal`

-- s 10(1): the common seal "must be in the custody of the Director".
-- (2): it "must not be affixed to any instrument except in the presence of -- (a) the Chairperson or a member of the Board
-- designated by the Chairperson; and (b) the Director or a member of the Executive Committee designated by the Director, and not
-- until the Chairperson or the member of the Board and the Director or the member of the Executive Committee have signed their
-- names to the instrument in token of their presence."
-- What follows for an instrument sealed otherwise (void, voidable, or merely irregular) the text does not say; "properly sealed"
-- here means only that s 10(2) was followed.
DECLARE BoardWitness IS ONE OF
    `the Chairperson`
    `a Board member designated by the Chairperson`
    `a Board member not designated by the Chairperson`
    `nobody from the Board`

DECLARE ManagementWitness IS ONE OF
    `the Director`
    `an Executive Committee member designated by the Director`
    `an Executive Committee member not designated by the Director`
    `a staff member not on the Executive Committee`

GIVEN `the Board-side witness` IS A BoardWitness
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board-side witness qualifies` IF
    CONSIDER `the Board-side witness`
    WHEN `the Chairperson` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Board member designated by the Chairperson` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the management-side witness` IS A ManagementWitness
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the management-side witness qualifies` IF
    CONSIDER `the management-side witness`
    WHEN `the Director` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an Executive Committee member designated by the Director` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the Board-side witness` IS A BoardWitness,
      `the management-side witness` IS A ManagementWitness,
      `both witnesses signed the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instrument is properly sealed` IF
        `the Board-side witness qualifies` `the Board-side witness`
    AND `the management-side witness qualifies` `the management-side witness`
    AND `both witnesses signed the instrument`

§§ `14(2)(d)(vii), (h) -- fees`

-- s 14(2): the Executive Committee's functions include "(d) the making, SUBJECT TO THE APPROVAL OF THE BOARD, of regulations
-- relating generally to the academic management of the Institute and in particular to -- ... (vii) the fees to be payable at
-- the Institute" and "(h) the demand and receipt of any fees that may from time to time be prescribed by regulations".
-- s 2: "regulations" means regulations made by the Executive Committee under section 14.
-- Reading (h) with (d)(vii), a fee may be demanded only if regulations prescribe it, and those regulations need the Board's
-- approval. That (d)(vii)'s approval requirement governs every fee regulation is an inference; (h) itself does not repeat it.
GIVEN `the fee is prescribed by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Board approved the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Institute may demand the fee` IF
        `the fee is prescribed by regulations`
    AND `the Board approved the regulations`

§§ `14(4) -- inspection of committee proceedings`

-- s 14(3): the Executive Committee may appoint committees "from among its own number".
-- (4): "The proceedings of every committee must be recorded in writing and must be open to inspection to any member of the
-- Executive Committee or any member of the committee at any time."
-- No one else is given a right of inspection by the Act -- not a Board member who is off the Executive Committee, not a fellow,
-- not the public. (Whether another law gives one is outside this encoding.)
DECLARE Inspector IS ONE OF
    `a member of the Executive Committee`
    `a member of the committee`
    `a Board member not on the Executive Committee`
    `a fellow of the Institute`
    `a member of the public`

GIVEN `the person asking` IS A Inspector
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may inspect the committee's proceedings under the Act` IF
    CONSIDER `the person asking`
    WHEN `a member of the Executive Committee` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a member of the committee` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `5, 5A, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15 -- who decides what`

-- s 5: the Board has power "(a) to receive and approve the annual report and accounts ...; (b) to approve the budget and research
-- programme". s 5A: the Minister may give the Institute directions under s 5 of the Public Sector (Governance) Act 2018.
-- s 11(1): "The Minister may authorise the payment of grants-in-aid". s 12(2): the Director is responsible for "(d) the discipline
-- of the fellows of the Institute". s 12(3), (4): the Board may appoint an acting Director, and "any other officers, employees,
-- consultants and agents". s 14(2): the Executive Committee's functions include "(b) the preparation of an annual report",
-- "(c) the appointment of the senior research staff and the senior administrative staff", and "(g) ... the welfare and discipline
-- of staff and fellows". s 15(1): "The Minister may make any rules that may be necessary"; (3) published in the Gazette and
-- presented to Parliament.
-- The discipline of fellows is given both to the Director (s 12(2)(d)) and, with the welfare and discipline of staff, to the
-- Executive Committee (s 14(2)(g)); the text does not reconcile the two. This encoding returns the Director, the more specific
-- provision, and says so: that choice is an inference.
DECLARE Matter IS ONE OF
    `approving the annual report and accounts`
    `preparing the annual report`
    `approving the budget and research programme`
    `appointing senior research staff`
    `appointing other officers and employees`
    `appointing an acting Director`
    `disciplining a fellow`
    `authorising grants-in-aid`
    `giving the Institute directions`
    `making rules under the Act`

DECLARE Body IS ONE OF
    `the Board`
    `the Executive Committee`
    `the Director`
    `the Minister`

GIVEN `the matter` IS A Matter
GIVETH A Body
DECIDE `who decides` IS
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `approving the annual report and accounts` THEN `the Board`
    WHEN `preparing the annual report` THEN `the Executive Committee`
    WHEN `approving the budget and research programme` THEN `the Board`
    WHEN `appointing senior research staff` THEN `the Executive Committee`
    WHEN `appointing other officers and employees` THEN `the Board`
    WHEN `appointing an acting Director` THEN `the Board`
    WHEN `disciplining a fellow` THEN `the Director`
    WHEN `authorising grants-in-aid` THEN `the Minister`
    WHEN `giving the Institute directions` THEN `the Minister`
    WHEN `making rules under the Act` THEN `the Minister`

§ `ISEAS - Yusof Ishak Institute Act 1968 -- the Board and the Executive Committee`

§§ `4 -- membership of the Board`

-- s 4(2): "The Board consists of a Chairperson, a Deputy Chairperson and 12 other members to be appointed by the Minister."
-- (3): "The Director is an ex-officio member of the Board." So the full Board is 1 + 1 + 12 + 1 = 15.
-- (4): appointed members "hold office for a period of up to 3 years, unless the Minister otherwise directs, and are eligible for
-- re-appointment". (5): the Minister "may at any time revoke an appointment".
-- (6): a member may resign "by giving written notice to that effect addressed to the Chairperson and as from the date the
-- Chairperson receives the notice the member ceases to be a member".
-- (9): "Any member absent from 4 consecutive meetings of the Board without having obtained leave of absence from the Board is
-- considered as having resigned".
-- (10): a person appointed to fill a vacancy "holds office for so long as the member in whose place the person is appointed would
-- have held office".
-- (11): "The Board must meet at least once a year."
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the full Board's size` IS 1 + 1 + 12 + 1

GIVEN `term in years` IS A NUMBER, `the Minister directed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the term is within s 4(4)` IF
        `term in years` <= 3
    OR  `the Minister directed otherwise`

GIVEN `gave written notice addressed to the Chairperson` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Chairperson has received the notice` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `consecutive meetings missed without leave` IS A NUMBER,
      `the Minister revoked the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member has ceased to be a member` IF
        (`gave written notice addressed to the Chairperson` AND `the Chairperson has received the notice`)
    OR  `consecutive meetings missed without leave` >= 4
    OR  `the Minister revoked the appointment`

GIVEN `predecessor's term in years` IS A NUMBER, `years the predecessor served` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `years the replacement holds office` IS
    `predecessor's term in years` - `years the predecessor served`

§§ `6 -- quorum and voting at Board meetings`

-- s 6(1): "Every question before the Board at any meeting is to be decided by a majority of the votes of the members present."
-- (2): "Five members of the Board constitute a quorum". (3): the person chairing "has an original vote and, in the case of an
-- equality of votes, a casting vote". s 4(7): if the Chairperson is absent, "the Deputy Chairperson must chair the meeting".
-- Reading "a majority of the votes" as a majority of the votes cast (the casting vote on an equality points that way) is an
-- inference. The votes counted below include the chair's original vote.
GIVEN `members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board meeting is quorate` IF `members present` >= 5

GIVEN `members at the meeting` IS A NUMBER, `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER, `the chair casts for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board question is carried` IF
        `the Board meeting is quorate` `members at the meeting`
    AND (    `votes for` > `votes against`
         OR  (`votes for` = `votes against` AND `the chair casts for`))

§§ `13 -- the Executive Committee`

-- s 13(2): the Executive Committee consists of "(a) the Director, who is its chairperson; (b) 3 members to be appointed by the
-- Board from among the members of the Board; (c) 3 members to be appointed by the Minister; and (d) 3 members to be appointed by
-- the Director from among the staff of the Institute" -- 1 + 3 + 3 + 3 = 10.
-- (4): "Five members of the Committee form a quorum at any meeting."
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the full Executive Committee's size` IS 1 + 3 + 3 + 3

GIVEN `committee members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Executive Committee meeting is quorate` IF `committee members present` >= 5
